The fast-path serve HAS sophisticated handoff detection: a grant-handoff bit (14289, edge-triggered, under-fires on TCP) and a **level-triggered epoch-adopt** (14351, gated on `mxfs_dir_epoch_adopt`). The epoch-adopt is the robust one but reads `dir_epoch` (=0, the dead signal). Let me check `mxfs_dir_epoch_adopt`'s default and confirm the epoch is the blocker.
`mxfs_dir_epoch_adopt=1` (on) but inert because `dir_epoch`=0. The whole chain converges on: **the modifying node reads its own `lk->dir_epoch`=0** even though the master computes epoch→515. I need to see why `mxfs_dlm_grant_dir_epoch` returns 0 for ino=131. Let me add a direct probe there and enlarge the shadow table (a plausible overflow source) in one build.
